      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Gratiot County Courthouse, a masterfully preserved landmark, sits on a lawn that hosts the Gratiot All Wars Memorial Monument.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Ithaca_(Michigan)",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Ithaca Fire Hall, once the original Village Hall, now serves as a museum and is connected to the Police Department.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Ithaca_(Michigan)",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Great Lakes Central Railroad bisects Ithaca, used predominantly for freight service, a reminder of the town’s rail heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
